  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 385, the Treasury distinguishes debt from equity using factors including a written unconditional promise to repay, a fixed maturity date, a reasonable interest rate, and the debt-to-equity ratio. A fixed maturity date and repayment obligation are hallmarks of true indebtedness.
Wrong (A): The physical appearance of a certificate has no bearing on the debt-versus-equity analysis.
