  choices = $EXPL$["The debt exceeds equity by more than the safe-harbor 3:1 ratio","The 10:1 debt-to-equity ratio suggests recharacterization as equity","All shareholder loans are automatically recharacterized as equity","The stated interest rate on the loan is below market"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Sec. 385, the IRS may recharacterize purported debt as equity when the debt-to-equity ratio is excessive. A 10:1 ratio strongly suggests the instrument lacks the economic substance of true indebtedness, converting deductible interest into nondeductible dividends.
Wrong (A): There is no statutory 3:1 safe-harbor ratio; courts examine all facts and circumstances under Sec. 385.
Wrong (C): Shareholder loans are not automatically recharacterized; the IRS must demonstrate that the instrument is equity in substance.
Wrong (D): While a below-market rate is one factor, the stem identifies the excessive ratio as the basis for the challenge.$EXPL$
