  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 7872, below-market loans between corporations and shareholders trigger imputed interest. The corporation is deemed to pay interest at the AFR (potentially deductible subject to Sec. 163(j)), and the shareholder is deemed to receive taxable interest income.
Wrong (A): A 0% interest loan between a shareholder and corporation is a below-market loan with mandatory imputed interest under Sec. 7872.
Wrong (C): The loan is not automatically recharacterized as a capital contribution; Sec. 7872 imputes interest rather than reclassifying the principal.
Wrong (D): Gift tax rules under Sec. 7872 apply to loans between individuals, not corporation-shareholder loans, which are treated as distributions.$EXPL$
