-- Q4369: Nontaxable Dispositions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["All deferred gain is recognized on the decedent''s final return","Obligation passes to heir with no gain recognition at death","The obligation is cancelled and all remaining gain is forgiven","The heir must pay all remaining tax within 90 days of death"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 453B(c), transfer of an installment obligation at death is not treated as a disposition. The estate or heir receives the obligation with the decedent''s basis and reports gain as payments are collected. Related party sales may trigger acceleration under Sec. 453(e).
Wrong (A): Death does not trigger immediate recognition of all deferred gain; Sec. 453B(c) specifically exempts transfers at death from disposition treatment.
Wrong (C): The obligation is not cancelled or forgiven; it remains enforceable and the heir continues to collect and report gain on payments.
Wrong (D): There is no 90-day payment requirement; the heir reports gain as installment payments are actually received.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4369;

-- Q4371: Nontaxable Dispositions [hard/L2]
