  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): A taxpayer may use both Section 121 and Section 1033 for a condemned principal residence. The Section 121 exclusion ($250,000/$500,000) reduces the gain first, and any remaining gain may then be deferred under Section 1033 by reinvesting in replacement property within the replacement period.
Wrong (A): The two provisions are not mutually exclusive; IRS guidance permits applying both sequentially to the same transaction.
Wrong (B): Section 1033 is not the only available provision; Section 121 also applies when the property qualifies as a principal residence.
