UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["It eliminates all state income tax obligations for the owners","It converts the owners'' ordinary income into capital gains","Owners may already deduct unlimited state taxes without a PTE election","The entity pays state tax and owners get a credit, bypassing the SALT cap"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under a PTE tax election, the entity pays state income tax at the entity level, reducing federal pass-through income. Individual owners receive a corresponding state credit or income exclusion, effectively allowing state tax deductions above the $10,000 SALT cap at the federal level.
Wrong (A): The election does not eliminate state tax; owners still bear the economic cost through reduced pass-through income or direct state credit mechanisms.
Wrong (B): The PTE election does not change income character; pass-through income retains its ordinary or capital nature under federal law.
Wrong (C): Without the PTE election, individual owners are subject to the $10,000 SALT cap under Sec. 164(b)(6) and cannot deduct unlimited state taxes.$EXPL$
