-- Q4994: Entity Formation and Restructuring [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Target is deemed to sell all assets at FMV on its final return","Target''s historical tax attributes carry over to the acquirer","The transaction qualifies as a tax-free reorganization","The acquirer recognizes gain on its stock purchase"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sec. 338(h)(10), the target corporation is treated as having sold all assets at fair market value in a deemed asset sale, with gain or loss recognized on old target''s final return. The target then receives a stepped-up basis in assets equal to the deemed purchase price.
Wrong (B): A 338(h)(10) election does not carry over historical tax attributes; the deemed asset sale creates a new tax basis, and prior attributes like NOLs are generally eliminated.
Wrong (C): A 338(h)(10) election is a taxable transaction, not a tax-free reorganization; gain is recognized at the corporate level.
Wrong (D): Under a 338(h)(10) election, the acquirer does not recognize gain on the stock purchase; the tax consequences are treated as an asset acquisition.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4994;

-- Q4995: Entity Formation and Restructuring [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Control of at least 50% of voting power or 50% of total stock value","Ownership of at least 80% of the transferee''s voting stock","Full 100% ownership of the transferee corporation","No minimum ownership requirement for Type D reorganizations"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 368(a)(1)(D), a divisive Type D reorganization requires control of the transferee, defined under Section 304(c) as ownership of at least 50% of total voting power or 50% of total value of stock by the transferor or its shareholders.
Wrong (B): The 80% threshold applies to Type B and Type C reorganizations under Section 368(c), not to divisive Type D reorganizations which use the 50% standard.
Wrong (C): Full 100% ownership is not required; the statute sets the threshold at 50% of voting power or value.
Wrong (D): A minimum ownership requirement does exist; without 50% control of the transferee, the transaction cannot qualify as a Type D reorganization.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4995;

-- Q4998: Entity Formation and Restructuring [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["A 338(g) is available only for affiliated group targets","A 338(g) eliminates all gain recognition on the acquisition","A 338(g) applies only to tax-free reorganization transactions","A 338(g) creates double tax at both shareholder and corporate levels"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 338(g), the stock purchase is treated as a taxable event. The selling shareholders recognize gain on the stock sale, and the deemed asset sale at the target level also triggers corporate-level gain, potentially resulting in double taxation. A 338(h)(10) election avoids this by treating the transaction as a single-level asset sale.
Wrong (A): A 338(g) election is not limited to affiliated group members; it is available for any qualified stock purchase. The 338(h)(10) election requires the target to be in a consolidated or affiliated group or be an S corporation.
Wrong (B): A 338(g) election does not eliminate gain; it creates a deemed asset sale that generates corporate-level gain in addition to shareholder-level gain.
Wrong (C): A 338(g) election applies to taxable stock purchases, not tax-free reorganizations.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4998;

-- Q4999: Entity Formation and Restructuring [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Retain at least 80% of the target''s employees for two years","Continue the target''s business or use its historic assets in a business","Maintain the target as a separate subsidiary for at least one year","File a continuity certification with the IRS within 90 days"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Treas. Reg. 1.368-1(d), the continuity of business enterprise (COBE) doctrine requires the acquirer to either continue the target''s historic business or use a significant portion of the target''s historic business assets in a business. Meeting either prong satisfies the requirement.
Wrong (A): COBE does not impose a specific employee retention percentage; the test focuses on the business or assets, not workforce headcount.
Wrong (C): There is no requirement to maintain the target as a separate subsidiary; the assets may be fully integrated into the acquirer''s operations.
Wrong (D): No continuity certification filing requirement exists; COBE is evaluated based on the acquirer''s actual post-reorganization conduct.$EXPL$
